component bsplit """Fan B's single joint command out to two stepgens, and gate one.

B is TWO CHUCKS. Each has its own worm gear and its own stepper (operator
2026-08-17). They are mirrored in the scales -- stepgen.00 scale +, stepgen.01
scale - (ned5_b.hal:45,55) -- so one command turns both the same way. What
couples them is the WORKPIECE held between them, nothing else.

WHY THIS EXISTS. Operator 2026-08-14: "I want in the UI an option to lock
either side of the B joint ... if unlocked, selecting LEFT or RIGHT JOGS one
or the other ... this lets me preload and helps align shit."

HOW ONE SIDE SITS OUT. By stopping its STEPS, not by moving its command.
Both cmd_l and cmd_r are ALWAYS equal to cmd; the deselected side is gated at
hm2_7i97.0.stepgen.NN.enable instead. A disabled hostmot2 stepgen zeroes its
step rate and ADOPTS position-cmd every cycle (stepgen.c:334-337), so it emits
nothing while gated and has nothing pending when it comes back -- there is no
jump and no slew to protect against.

The drive itself never sees that pin: ENA+- is left open, so it stays
energised and holding whatever the stepgen does (mesa_7i85s_wiring.md).

WHY NOT AN OFFSET. It used to hold the deselected side's OUTPUT still and
carry the difference in a realtime variable. That variable survives e-stop,
machine-off, R4 and drive power -- nothing clears a realtime variable except
unloading the component. So the two chucks stayed commanded apart forever, and
on 2026-08-17 that reached 22 deg at the joint (1.22 turns at the motor). With
a bar clamped in both chucks they twist against each other and stall, the
drives fault, and only a PB restart cleared it. The preload does not need
software's memory: each worm is self-locking and holds its own chuck with the
70 V brick dead (components.md:50).

SPLIT IS ACCOUNTING, NOT A COMMAND. `split` accumulates the joint motion the
gated side did not receive. It feeds nothing -- no command, no feedback, no
limit -- so it cannot fault anything, and zeroing or keeping it has no
mechanical consequence. There is no encoder on either chuck; this is a tally of
steps withheld, not a measurement.

ONLY THE RIGHT IS EVER GATED. The GUI toggle is two-state, L+R and L
(ned_controls.py B_SIDES), so joint.6.motor-pos-fb always comes off a live
stepgen and a real STEPGEN_MAXACCEL/MAXVEL clip still raises a genuine
following error -- the only check an axis with no encoder and no drive alarm
line has.""";

pin in float cmd "joint.6.motor-pos-cmd -- the single command LinuxCNC issues";
pin in signed sel = 0 "1 = LEFT only (RIGHT gated); anything else = BOTH";
pin in bit power "sig-b-servo-on -- b.pwr.and, the brick is live and settled";

pin in float fb_l "hm2_7i97.0.stepgen.00.position-fb -- steps the FPGA SENT";

pin out float cmd_l "-> hm2_7i97.0.stepgen.00.position-cmd (LEFT)";
pin out float cmd_r "-> hm2_7i97.0.stepgen.01.position-cmd (RIGHT), always == cmd_l";
pin out bit en_l "-> hm2_7i97.0.stepgen.00.enable";
pin out bit en_r "-> hm2_7i97.0.stepgen.01.enable -- FALSE while LEFT-only";
pin out float fb "-> joint.6.motor-pos-fb";
pin out float split "joint degrees the gated side did not receive -- READOUT ONLY";

/* prev is last cycle's cmd, used only to tally what the gated side missed. */
variable double prev = 0.0;
variable int started = 0;

function _ "Fan the joint command to both stepgens; gate the deselected one";
license "GPL";
;;

FUNCTION(_) {
    /* First pass: outputs start exactly where the command is and both sides
       start gated, so inserting this component into a running machine cannot
       move anything. */
    if (!started) {
        cmd_l = cmd;
        cmd_r = cmd;
        en_l = 0;
        en_r = 0;
        fb = fb_l;
        split = 0.0;
        prev = cmd;
        started = 1;
        return;
    }

    /* THE COMMANDS NEVER DIVERGE. This is the whole fix: there is no offset
       to accumulate, so there is nothing to persist and nothing to reconcile
       when the gated side is reselected. */
    cmd_l = cmd;
    cmd_r = cmd;

    en_l = power;
    en_r = power && (sel != 1);

    /* Accounting only. Tally while the RIGHT is gated BY SELECTION -- when
       power is down both sides are dead and neither chuck moves, so there is
       nothing to withhold. */
    if (power && sel == 1) {
        split += (cmd - prev);
    }
    prev = cmd;

    fb = fb_l;
}
